r David.**.\n   - This means if a student is working in the lab, they are instructed by professor David.\n\n6. **James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - From point 5, James is instructed by professor David.\n   - From point 4, James is taking the database course.\n   - From point 3, James is from the computer science department.\n\n7. **Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.**.\n   - This information about Jack is not directly relevant to James.\n\nNow, let\'s determine if James has a part-time job offered by the university:.\n- From point 2, if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must work in the library.\n- From point 1, if a student works in the library, they are not from the computer science department.\n- James is from the computer science department (point 6).\n\nSince James is from the computer science department, he cannot work in the library (point 1). Therefore, James cannot have a part-time job offered by the university (point 2).\n\nThus, the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is **True**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
