ab are instructed by professor David.**.\n   - This means if a student is working in the lab, they are instructed by professor David.\n\n6. **James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - From point 5, James is instructed by professor David.\n   - From point 4, since James is instructed by professor David, he is taking the database course.\n   - From point 3, since James is taking the database course, he is from the computer science department.\n   - From point 1, since James is from the computer science department, he cannot work in the library.\n   - From point 2, since James cannot work in the library, he cannot have a part-time job offered by the university.\n\n7. **Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.**.\n   - This information about Jack is not relevant to determining James\'s situation.\n\nBased on the logical deductions above, we can conclude that James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
