 more, the security deposit at the Olive Garden could be $2000 or more.\n\nHowever, Tom\'s condition states that he will rent an apartment only if the security deposit is no more than $1500. Since $2000 is more than $1500, Tom will not rent an apartment at the Olive Garden based on his condition.\n\nThe question asks if the following statement is true, false, or uncertain: "The security deposit at the Olive Garden is either $2000 or more.".\n\nBased on the information provided, the security deposit can be $2000 or more, but Tom\'s condition implies that he will not rent an apartment if the deposit is more than $1500. This does not affect the fact that the deposit can be $2000 or more.\n\nTherefore, the statement "The security deposit at the Olive Garden is either $2000 or more" is true. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
