.\n   - This confirms that the minimum security deposit (equal to one month\'s rent) is $2000, which is more than $1500.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the conditions for Tom to rent an apartment in The Olive Garden:.\n\n- **Condition 1:** Tom is allowed to move in with Fluffy.\n  - We do not have information about whether The Olive Garden allows pets. Therefore, this condition is uncertain.\n\n- **Condition 2:** The security deposit is no more than $1500.\n  - The minimum security deposit is $2000, which is more than $1500. Therefore, this condition is false.\n\nSince one of the conditions (Condition 2) is false, Tom will not rent an apartment in The Olive Garden.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Tom will rent an apartment in The Olive Garden" is **False**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
