ightarrow C \\), we can deduce that \\( C \\) is true (George can compose).\n   - Now, we have both \\( C \\) and \\( W \\) as true. From \\( (C \\land W) \\rightarrow A \\), we can deduce that \\( A \\) is true (George will compose).\n\n6. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Based on the given information and logical deductions, if George likes music and has access to a program, he will compose.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
