er (because all basketball players are tall).\n\nGiven this analysis, the statement "If Yuri is not an American basketball player, then Yuri is a basketball player" is inherently contradictory because Yuri cannot be a basketball player at all (regardless of nationality).\n\nTherefore, the statement is **False**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
